                "id": "rd_14",
                "title": "Reading Test 14: Renewable Energy Innovations",
                "text": "<p class=\"mb-4\">The transition from fossil fuels to renewable energy sources is imperative for mitigating catastrophic climate change. While solar and wind power have seen massive adoption, their intermittent nature remains a significant hurdle. Consequently, recent innovations have heavily focused on advanced energy storage solutions, aiming to capture excess energy generated during peak conditions for use when the sun isn't shining or the wind isn't blowing.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">One prominent area of innovation is the development of next-generation batteries. Beyond the standard lithium-ion technology, researchers are exploring solid-state batteries and flow batteries, which promise higher energy densities, longer lifespans, and improved safety profiles. Furthermore, green hydrogen is emerging as a potential game-changer. By using surplus renewable electricity to split water into hydrogen and oxygen, energy can be stored and later burned without emitting carbon.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">Another frontier is the modernization of the electrical grid. Smart grids utilize AI and IoT sensors to dynamically balance supply and demand in real-time, integrating distributed energy resources like rooftop solar panels and electric vehicles. These interconnected technologies are slowly building a resilient, decentralized energy infrastructure capable of sustaining a zero-carbon future.</p>",
